{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"825c (ruinable-cozey-caracal) UNPARENTED from epic 2ddd and force-closed by operator decision: it is not a consolidation. Its three 'copies' of the close-reason/force rule differ in four material ways, decisively CLI-refuses vs library-silently-discards, both pinned - so no merge leaves the suite green and converging either way is a deliberate behaviour change. It would also have violated the epic's own consolidation guarantees (changes pinned behaviour on two surfaces; net additive). Analysis preserved as ticket comments. Residual filed as e1a2-0a03-e26b-416e (unthinking-halfwoolen-anura), linked discovered_from 2ddd: MCP transition_ticket still lacks 'reason' and its strict-xfail row cites scratchy-leprous-galago, which is CLOSED - so the live gap had no open tracker. Also recorded there: adapters.py:442 classifies by signature INTROSPECTION, so a signature-only addition would flip the strict-xfail to xpass while the datum is still discarded."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787374903554908001,"uuid":"9ddb36eb-51f8-4fe4-8991-719c8d7948e5"}